or neurosurgeons or cardiac surgeons are among the most highly compensated physicians compared to, say, family medicine or pediatrics or, say, general internal medicine, these primary care physicians who spend most of their time counseling patients and helping to prevent disease, encouraging them to stop smoking, lose weight, focus on vaccinations, focus on healthy diets.

21
00:11:50.000 --> 00:12:09.000
None of those are really very profitable right now in a fee-for-service system. And the ironic thing is, at the end of this, it's also antithetical to what patients want, because ultimately, if I'm with a patient, what I really want is to be as healthy as possible with minimal contact with the healthcare system. Well, that may be true,

22
