400,000 people per year by some reports. And these are definitely disputed. It's not clear again. Nobody writes medical mistake on the death certificate, for example. But some people have estimated that it is the third leading cause of death in this country. I mean, that is just astonishing, Vivian, that the idea that medical mistakes might rival the consequences of cigarette smoking. I mean, that's just, I mean, my jaw fell to the floor when I saw those numbers. It's, you know, it is very difficult and I am always a little bit conflicted when I talk

