there's no question that there are a significant number of medical mistakes that do take place in this country, even if we don't know for sure what the total is. How are medical mistakes shaped by the fee-for-service system that we've built? Well, one of the issues when you have a fever service system is that you are incentivizing over treatment, over diagnosis, even if the physicians themselves or the clinician themselves are really doing their very best. You are in a system that, for example, if you have any doubt about a person who has, let's say, a headache

