profound admiration for most, if not all, of my colleagues in healthcare. But I think the system is really failing us. really failing us. And it's easy, I think, when we walk into, you know, gleaming healthcare facilities to imagine that these are places that are flush with money, but it turns out that that's not the case, right? Many hospital systems are actually almost on life support themselves. That's another really surprising statistic, I think, for most people that the average profit margin

53
