or to take risk. The COVID pandemic has made many of the problems with our system transparent. Hospital systems that depend on providing services to stay solvent are on the verge of bankruptcy as elective procedures have dried up. Frontline medical workers have found themselves with our basic protective equipment. A system not geared toward prevention quickly became overwhelmed as the virus surged.

55
